WEBVTT

1
00:01:45.106 --> 00:01:48.981
ON APRIL 26, 1986, REACTOR NO. 4
OF THE CHERNOBYL NUCLEAR POWER PLANT

2
00:01:49.064 --> 00:01:51.314
SUFFERED A CATASTROPHIC EXPLOSION,

3
00:01:51.397 --> 00:01:56.022
CAUSING ONE OF THE LARGEST MAN-MADE
DISASTERS IN THE HISTORY OF MANKIND.

4
00:01:56.106 --> 00:02:01.939
THIS FILM IS INSPIRED
BY REAL EVENTS.

5
00:02:02.064 --> 00:02:08.772
THE FILM'S CHARACTERS AND THEIR
LIFE STORIES ARE FICTIONAL.

6
00:02:33.772 --> 00:02:35.606
-Thank you.
-I'll get you the change.

7
00:02:35.689 --> 00:02:37.106
-No, keep it.
-Thank you.

8
00:02:38.606 --> 00:02:40.689
-Come with me.
-I'm busy.

9
00:02:40.772 --> 00:02:44.189
-Some firemen came in. Pick one.
-This is not a dating agency.

10
00:02:44.272 --> 00:02:45.606
You need a man.

11
00:02:45.689 --> 00:02:48.106
-No, I don't.
-You do, more than anyone.

12
00:02:58.106 --> 00:02:59.356
There they are.

13
00:03:06.064 --> 00:03:07.272
I have to go home.

14
00:03:07.356 --> 00:03:09.856
But there's a huge line
of customers waiting outside.

15
00:03:14.939 --> 00:03:18.314
-I'm sorry, I have to go.
-Girls, are you on strike or something?

16
00:03:19.189 --> 00:03:20.189
Come on in.

17
00:03:20.772 --> 00:03:22.189
-Where do I sit?
-Over there.

18
00:03:44.189 --> 00:03:45.397
Hello, Alex.

19
00:03:46.897 --> 00:03:47.897
Hello, Olga.

20
00:03:48.939 --> 00:03:50.564
Have you two met before?

21
00:03:54.606 --> 00:03:55.606
More than ten years ago.

22
00:03:58.814 --> 00:04:00.897
Just don't cut both my ears off, okay?

23
00:04:02.022 --> 00:04:02.856
One will do.

24
00:04:11.856 --> 00:04:13.481
I thought you were in Kiev.

25
00:04:15.189 --> 00:04:17.022
And I thought you were in Kiev, too.

26
00:04:19.814 --> 00:04:22.356
-You haven't changed.
-Liar.

27
00:04:50.981 --> 00:04:51.981
ENTRANCE

28
00:04:55.481 --> 00:04:56.314
Olga…

29
00:04:57.856 --> 00:04:59.814
Come ride with me, for old times' sake.

30
00:05:01.272 --> 00:05:02.606
Just like that?

31
00:05:02.689 --> 00:05:05.564
I could send a formal request,
but it might take until winter.

32
00:05:06.856 --> 00:05:10.147
-Come back in three weeks for a trim.
-Olga, the bus is coming.

33
00:05:32.356 --> 00:05:34.064
Move over, granny.

34
00:05:36.897 --> 00:05:39.189
Dressed up like dollar prostitutes.

35
00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:41.106
That's exactly what we are.

36
00:05:42.189 --> 00:05:43.272
Jesus.

37
00:05:54.272 --> 00:05:56.981
Close your legs, you're not at work.

38
00:06:13.106 --> 00:06:17.022
What's your problem?
Most women would kill for a man like that.

39
00:06:23.522 --> 00:06:24.981
Open the door!

40
00:06:28.231 --> 00:06:30.147
Sorry about that, everyone.

41
00:06:31.189 --> 00:06:32.439
Olga.

42
00:06:33.647 --> 00:06:36.689
Come with me or these
passengers will be stuck here all day.

43
00:06:40.147 --> 00:06:42.231
Miss, you're holding us up.

44
00:06:49.981 --> 00:06:51.981
-Bye, everyone.
-Good riddance.

45
00:07:17.772 --> 00:07:19.231
Well, what do you want?

46
00:07:21.356 --> 00:07:22.439
Nothing.

47
00:07:34.106 --> 00:07:35.397
I want to hug you.

48
00:07:41.106 --> 00:07:42.022
Go on then.

49
00:08:12.606 --> 00:08:14.022
Like a couple of pensioners.

50
00:08:15.397 --> 00:08:16.397
Hi, Olga.

51
00:08:18.231 --> 00:08:19.189
Hi, Alex.

52
00:08:26.106 --> 00:08:28.397
Come on, where do you want to go?

53
00:08:29.231 --> 00:08:32.231
You pulled me off the bus,
so let's hear your suggestions.

54
00:08:33.397 --> 00:08:36.731
Let's go to a restaurant?
Or how about we head into Kiev?

55
00:08:39.022 --> 00:08:42.981
Remember when we had no money,
we shared one ice cream between us?

56
00:08:44.564 --> 00:08:48.231
-Got it. We need an ice cream.
-Two ice creams.

57
00:08:57.397 --> 00:08:58.981
Excuse me, I'm in a terrible rush.

58
00:08:59.064 --> 00:09:02.189
-How many?
-Two. Nice hair, by the way.

59
00:09:02.272 --> 00:09:04.439
ICE CREAM

60
00:09:04.522 --> 00:09:06.231
-Here you are.
-Thank you.

61
00:09:11.189 --> 00:09:13.022
Let's go for a ride on the Ferris wheel?

62
00:09:13.106 --> 00:09:15.106
It won't be open until May Day.

63
00:09:15.189 --> 00:09:19.064
My buddies from the local fire station
did the safety inspection on it.

64
00:09:19.147 --> 00:09:22.064
We can get a private test ride.

65
00:09:22.856 --> 00:09:26.064
-You're just as crazy as when you were 20.
-Who, me? Not at all.

66
00:10:17.856 --> 00:10:19.647
This is far enough. Stop here.

67
00:10:24.606 --> 00:10:26.064
Thanks for the ride.

68
00:10:47.189 --> 00:10:48.939
It was a nice evening, thank you.

69
00:10:49.814 --> 00:10:51.564
What about the cake we bought?

70
00:10:53.856 --> 00:10:55.731
Pulling out your nuclear weapon?

71
00:10:56.272 --> 00:10:58.106
Atomic power to the masses.

72
00:11:00.147 --> 00:11:01.231
I'll pass.

73
00:11:10.939 --> 00:11:13.397
Olga! Wait.

74
00:11:14.564 --> 00:11:16.022
Alex, some other time, okay?

75
00:11:17.981 --> 00:11:19.689
Greetings, fellas! What's the occasion?

76
00:11:20.606 --> 00:11:22.564
Celebrating Soviet technical prowess.

77
00:11:23.481 --> 00:11:25.564
You got a husband in there or something?

78
00:11:25.647 --> 00:11:27.022
No, why?

79
00:11:31.564 --> 00:11:33.147
I promise, no funny business.

80
00:11:33.231 --> 00:11:35.147
I just don't want to say goodbye yet.

81
00:11:37.272 --> 00:11:39.314
I haven't had such a good time in ages.

82
00:11:40.564 --> 00:11:43.189
But you have
a different life now, and so do I.

83
00:11:44.064 --> 00:11:46.522
We can see each other
at the hair salon sometimes.

84
00:11:47.897 --> 00:11:49.772
Olga, my hair grows too slowly.

85
00:11:50.564 --> 00:11:51.397
Bye.

86
00:12:05.647 --> 00:12:07.814
I'm home. How's it going?

87
00:12:09.439 --> 00:12:10.731
I don't like this school.

88
00:12:11.689 --> 00:12:13.272
You'll make friends soon.

89
00:12:13.356 --> 00:12:15.439
They're all scientists' kids,

90
00:12:15.522 --> 00:12:16.606
little smartasses.

91
00:12:17.606 --> 00:12:20.522
Olga?

92
00:12:21.356 --> 00:12:23.647
Olga, I forgot to give you the cake.

93
00:12:24.731 --> 00:12:26.564
-Olga?
-Stop shouting and go away.

94
00:12:26.647 --> 00:12:28.981
If you're ashamed
of your apartment, I live in a dorm.

95
00:12:29.064 --> 00:12:29.981
Go away.

96
00:12:37.856 --> 00:12:39.189
This is my son, Alex.

97
00:12:39.272 --> 00:12:40.439
Alex, this is uncle Alexey.

98
00:12:40.522 --> 00:12:42.022
Please be acquainted.

99
00:12:43.272 --> 00:12:44.356
Come in.

100
00:12:45.897 --> 00:12:48.147
Are you sure this is a good time?

101
00:12:48.231 --> 00:12:49.189
Come in.

102
00:12:53.314 --> 00:12:55.231
-Howdy, namesake.
-Hello.

103
00:12:57.772 --> 00:13:00.231
You two boys chat here
while I go and change.

104
00:13:04.106 --> 00:13:04.981
Who are you?

105
00:13:07.397 --> 00:13:12.106
Who am I? I'm… a sun keeper.

106
00:13:12.189 --> 00:13:13.356
How's that?

107
00:13:13.439 --> 00:13:14.772
Well, for 200,000 years,

108
00:13:14.856 --> 00:13:16.981
people ran around naked
with sticks and stones,

109
00:13:17.064 --> 00:13:19.314
and then we built
our own sun, and I look after it.

110
00:13:19.397 --> 00:13:22.147
I see. Everyone here works at the reactor.

111
00:13:22.231 --> 00:13:24.606
But only the best
work in the fire service.

112
00:13:26.481 --> 00:13:29.814
-But that's not working at the reactor.
-Ever heard of fire inspections?

113
00:13:29.897 --> 00:13:31.981
I've been
over every inch of all four reactors,

114
00:13:32.064 --> 00:13:33.856
and fixed lots of problems.

115
00:13:36.647 --> 00:13:39.481
-What do you have in here?
-Photos of our neighbors.

116
00:13:41.231 --> 00:13:43.397
These ones I know.

117
00:13:44.147 --> 00:13:45.939
But who's this? Is he from Kazakhstan?

118
00:13:46.814 --> 00:13:48.856
That's Jackie Chan, he's from Hong Kong.

119
00:13:48.939 --> 00:13:50.606
He's even tougher than Bruce Lee.

120
00:13:52.272 --> 00:13:55.689
-You're into filmmaking?
-This camera isn't good for that.

121
00:13:55.772 --> 00:13:57.356
It was my grandpa's.

122
00:14:01.939 --> 00:14:03.689
You boys got to know each other?

123
00:14:08.064 --> 00:14:09.439
Can I have a word with you?

124
00:14:19.439 --> 00:14:20.439
How old is he?

125
00:14:21.106 --> 00:14:21.939
He's ten.

126
00:14:24.231 --> 00:14:25.397
Whose is he?

127
00:14:27.231 --> 00:14:28.397
He's mine.

128
00:14:58.606 --> 00:14:59.939
Why didn't you tell me?

129
00:15:04.106 --> 00:15:06.522
How could I tell you
if I didn't even know where you were?

130
00:15:14.522 --> 00:15:17.231
-How's the cake?
-It conforms to state standards.

131
00:15:19.189 --> 00:15:20.689
I'll have a slice, too, then.

132
00:15:36.106 --> 00:15:37.522
Should we tell him?

133
00:15:40.397 --> 00:15:42.314
No need to tell him anything.

134
00:15:42.397 --> 00:15:43.439
Eat your cake.

135
00:16:10.606 --> 00:16:11.647
Right.

136
00:16:12.689 --> 00:16:14.689
What date is tomorrow?
The 12th? I have a day off.

137
00:16:14.772 --> 00:16:16.647
We're all going to Kiev for the day.

138
00:16:16.731 --> 00:16:19.231
I'll be here at 9:00 a.m.,
and I'm bringing presents.

139
00:16:19.897 --> 00:16:22.231
And then we'll have dinner
all together at home.

140
00:16:24.439 --> 00:16:25.731
All right?

141
00:16:29.897 --> 00:16:32.189
-Bye.
-I'm working tomorrow.

142
00:16:33.231 --> 00:16:34.772
Can't you get a day off?

143
00:16:38.772 --> 00:16:40.689
I guess I can switch with Marina.

144
00:16:41.272 --> 00:16:42.314
With Marina…

145
00:16:43.647 --> 00:16:45.731
Perfect. It's a date then.

146
00:16:48.022 --> 00:16:49.481
See you at 9:00 a.m. Sharp.

147
00:16:50.356 --> 00:16:51.814
I'll see myself out.

148
00:16:52.439 --> 00:16:53.314
Bye, Alex.

149
00:17:20.897 --> 00:17:24.314
TWO WEEKS LATER

150
00:17:26.189 --> 00:17:28.147
What can I say, my dear friends.

151
00:17:31.564 --> 00:17:33.981
It is with a heavy heart that I leave you.

152
00:17:34.064 --> 00:17:35.439
I gave you everything I have.

153
00:17:36.981 --> 00:17:42.856
My youth, wisdom, health, beauty,
and my hope for a better future.

154
00:17:44.022 --> 00:17:46.064
-Attention!
-As you were.

155
00:17:46.147 --> 00:17:47.439
You still owe me ten rubles.

156
00:17:47.522 --> 00:17:49.731
A materialist like you
can't be trusted with money.

157
00:17:49.814 --> 00:17:52.856
I'd give it back,
but you'll spend it on a soldering iron.

158
00:17:57.106 --> 00:17:58.689
What will you do without me?

159
00:17:59.272 --> 00:18:01.356
We'll finally put things in order.

160
00:18:01.439 --> 00:18:04.772
We know the drill, Comrade Colonel.
First breakfast, then lunch, then dinner.

161
00:18:05.564 --> 00:18:08.481
It's a solid foundation
for everything else,

162
00:18:08.564 --> 00:18:09.981
unlike your flimsy structure.

163
00:18:14.397 --> 00:18:16.022
Well, guys, keep your hoses dry.

164
00:18:25.564 --> 00:18:26.981
Go ahead, I'm ready.

165
00:18:41.022 --> 00:18:42.522
Do it!

166
00:18:56.356 --> 00:18:57.522
Alex!

167
00:19:01.481 --> 00:19:03.189
Come here, you!

168
00:19:35.481 --> 00:19:37.397
You have no respect for your elders.

169
00:19:39.356 --> 00:19:40.481
Is this Valery?

170
00:19:40.564 --> 00:19:42.939
Yep, my baby brother.

171
00:19:43.022 --> 00:19:45.814
-He's got a PhD, works at the reactor.
-Sergey, cut it out.

172
00:19:47.856 --> 00:19:49.106
Nice to meet you, Alexey.

173
00:19:49.731 --> 00:19:50.856
Likewise.

174
00:19:55.064 --> 00:19:56.189
Here it is.

175
00:19:57.814 --> 00:20:00.606
-Where's the box?
-What box? It's second-hand.

176
00:20:01.481 --> 00:20:03.814
You always need
to keep hold of the packaging.

177
00:20:03.897 --> 00:20:04.981
Let's see.

178
00:20:06.397 --> 00:20:08.314
Here, 500.

179
00:20:09.314 --> 00:20:11.564
-Count it.
-I'll take your word for it.

180
00:20:12.939 --> 00:20:15.147
Here's the camera.
In a box, as it should be.

181
00:20:15.939 --> 00:20:18.439
-I gave it a good cleaning.
-Much appreciated.

182
00:20:18.522 --> 00:20:20.564
And here's the manual.

183
00:20:24.772 --> 00:20:27.856
-Here's a bag.
-Handy.

184
00:20:31.022 --> 00:20:34.522
You're a good firefighter.
You should've stayed on.

185
00:20:34.606 --> 00:20:37.814
I'm just fed up wandering
around corridors checking stuff.

186
00:20:37.897 --> 00:20:39.731
That's part of the job. What do you want?

187
00:20:39.814 --> 00:20:41.689
I want to see Alla Pugacheva in concert.

188
00:20:43.272 --> 00:20:46.731
-She'll come here one day.
-So sit here and wait for her then.

189
00:20:46.814 --> 00:20:49.231
Valery, come
and join us in the dormitory later.

190
00:20:49.314 --> 00:20:52.272
I'm having a farewell party.
It'll be fun. See you then.

191
00:20:53.814 --> 00:20:55.481
See you later, Sergey.

192
00:21:04.522 --> 00:21:06.314
Are you coming or not?

193
00:21:28.064 --> 00:21:31.272
-But this is not Chanel.
-I'm not the Czechoslovakian ambassador.

194
00:21:39.939 --> 00:21:41.772
Bring it back in 24 hours.

195
00:21:42.397 --> 00:21:45.022
-But you said two days.
-And you said Chanel.

196
00:21:46.981 --> 00:21:48.106
You're breaking my heart.

197
00:21:56.314 --> 00:21:59.064
THE PARTY PLANS, WE MAKE IT HAPPEN

198
00:22:03.397 --> 00:22:05.356
WALL OF HONOR

199
00:22:25.939 --> 00:22:31.939
CHERNOBYL NPP

200
00:23:24.606 --> 00:23:26.731
Alex!

201
00:23:33.022 --> 00:23:35.106
-Hey.
-Hi.

202
00:23:38.314 --> 00:23:40.564
I brought you a present. Here.

203
00:23:40.647 --> 00:23:43.356
-What is it?
-A proper film camera.

204
00:23:44.481 --> 00:23:46.397
-No way. Really?
-Yes way, silly.

205
00:23:47.231 --> 00:23:48.481
It's a Lomo.

206
00:23:49.231 --> 00:23:51.939
-How did you get it?
-With a bit of perseverance.

207
00:23:52.564 --> 00:23:53.481
Wow.

208
00:23:54.689 --> 00:23:55.647
Thank you.

209
00:23:56.689 --> 00:23:58.272
Mom and I were waiting for you.

210
00:24:00.814 --> 00:24:03.647
Sorry. I got caught up with work.

211
00:24:06.856 --> 00:24:07.814
And here's the manual.

212
00:24:09.564 --> 00:24:10.689
Here.

213
00:24:13.106 --> 00:24:14.564
What should I tell Mom?

214
00:24:21.189 --> 00:24:23.314
Just tell her
that Father Christmas came early.

215
00:24:33.189 --> 00:24:34.481
See you later.

216
00:25:08.981 --> 00:25:10.647
I remember fire at the third reactor.

217
00:25:10.731 --> 00:25:13.897
We were all sweating like pigs,
could hardly keep hold of our hoses.

218
00:25:13.981 --> 00:25:17.481
Well, Alex stripped down
to his briefs, put his sunglasses on,

219
00:25:17.564 --> 00:25:20.272
and started wetting
the dry wall with buckets of water.

220
00:25:20.356 --> 00:25:21.356
A rainbow above him.

221
00:25:22.772 --> 00:25:26.606
All for Elena from HR,
who was watching him from her window.

222
00:25:27.731 --> 00:25:29.189
You're making stuff up.

223
00:25:29.272 --> 00:25:31.897
The whole brigade got a bonus,
and Alex was demoted to captain.

224
00:25:35.272 --> 00:25:37.064
Alex, I envy you, in a good way.

225
00:25:39.147 --> 00:25:41.689
I envy your freedom
and your willful heart.

226
00:25:43.897 --> 00:25:47.356
You're fearless, you do
as you please, and you answer to nobody.

227
00:25:48.064 --> 00:25:50.397
Well, keep your hose dry, buddy.

228
00:25:51.189 --> 00:25:52.606
-Hurrah!
-Hurrah!

229
00:25:54.147 --> 00:25:55.481
Thanks, Sergey.

230
00:26:07.439 --> 00:26:09.439
-Slow down, Alex.
-I'll be fine.

231
00:26:17.397 --> 00:26:18.814
Was that a made-up story?

232
00:26:23.772 --> 00:26:25.231
I'll be right back.

233
00:26:39.564 --> 00:26:41.981
-Why aren't you eating?
-I'll eat later.

234
00:26:44.981 --> 00:26:47.856
-Stop filming me.
-Stop stopping me.

235
00:26:51.356 --> 00:26:52.939
You'll have to give the camera back.

236
00:26:53.022 --> 00:26:54.647
But, Mom, it's a gift.

237
00:26:57.606 --> 00:26:58.772
I'll get it.

238
00:27:02.231 --> 00:27:03.564
It's Father Christmas!

239
00:27:04.439 --> 00:27:06.981
Alex! What's up?

240
00:27:10.147 --> 00:27:14.147
Damn it, Alex, look at you!

241
00:27:14.231 --> 00:27:16.897
What a little man? Just look at you.

242
00:27:16.981 --> 00:27:18.814
I just can't…

243
00:27:19.814 --> 00:27:20.689
Are you drunk?

244
00:27:22.772 --> 00:27:24.356
I'm drunk with love.

245
00:27:26.731 --> 00:27:28.022
Go play outside.

246
00:27:32.439 --> 00:27:35.356
Mom, can Uncle Alexey stay for dinner?

247
00:27:35.439 --> 00:27:37.856
That's none of your business. Go outside.

248
00:27:39.231 --> 00:27:40.231
Not fair.

249
00:27:46.606 --> 00:27:48.481
May I come in?

250
00:27:51.397 --> 00:27:53.231
Fried potatoes!

251
00:28:22.814 --> 00:28:24.022
Olga, please, I'm sorry.

252
00:28:25.731 --> 00:28:28.564
I got very sick, so sick…

253
00:28:30.356 --> 00:28:32.064
I was at death's door.

254
00:28:33.272 --> 00:28:34.981
Did some nurse save you?

255
00:28:43.772 --> 00:28:45.189
I'm moving to Kiev.

256
00:28:46.147 --> 00:28:47.939
I can't take it here anymore.

257
00:28:48.022 --> 00:28:50.814
I'm a top expert,
and I have nothing to do here.

258
00:28:50.897 --> 00:28:52.231
-Come with me.
-Stop it.

259
00:28:53.231 --> 00:28:54.147
Olga…

260
00:28:55.314 --> 00:28:56.439
come with me.

261
00:28:58.356 --> 00:29:01.897
I'll buy Alex a water pistol,
and we'll put fires out together.

262
00:29:03.731 --> 00:29:06.231
We were waiting
for you that day. I made dinner.

263
00:29:11.147 --> 00:29:12.689
I lied to my colleagues.

264
00:29:14.231 --> 00:29:15.897
I said I don't want to work here,

265
00:29:17.147 --> 00:29:18.356
that I want to leave.

266
00:29:18.439 --> 00:29:19.522
But the truth is…

267
00:29:21.064 --> 00:29:22.147
I just want to be with you.

268
00:29:24.731 --> 00:29:26.897
I don't want to hear any of it.

269
00:29:26.981 --> 00:29:30.439
No. I made up my mind. Really.

270
00:29:32.772 --> 00:29:34.897
I want a family with you.

271
00:29:39.147 --> 00:29:40.856
It's not going to work between us.

272
00:29:41.772 --> 00:29:42.772
Go on your own.

273
00:29:44.147 --> 00:29:45.856
Stop talking nonsense.

274
00:29:48.522 --> 00:29:49.772
Let's go together.

275
00:29:50.481 --> 00:29:54.064
We'll rent a place for a while,
and then apply to get our own apartment.

276
00:29:55.564 --> 00:29:57.272
We're not going anywhere with you.

277
00:29:58.231 --> 00:29:59.356
Leave us alone.

278
00:30:01.439 --> 00:30:03.689
Are you telling me to abandon Alex?

279
00:30:05.272 --> 00:30:07.606
We've been fine without you all this time.

280
00:30:47.647 --> 00:30:49.106
Listen, I'm really going to leave,

281
00:30:49.897 --> 00:30:50.856
and that'll be it.

282
00:30:52.647 --> 00:30:53.481
Forever.

283
00:30:56.689 --> 00:30:59.356
Just make sure
this time you leave for good.

284
00:31:12.189 --> 00:31:13.022
Fine.

285
00:31:14.231 --> 00:31:15.731
Good luck with your life.

286
00:31:23.814 --> 00:31:29.397
Leave.

287
00:31:56.647 --> 00:31:59.439
This is the best spot!
We can see everything from here!

288
00:32:10.814 --> 00:32:12.189
Let's get closer!

289
00:32:17.064 --> 00:32:18.689
Get the camera.

290
00:32:30.314 --> 00:32:32.814
It's too dark
for your camera to record anything.

291
00:32:44.189 --> 00:32:47.606
Our folks will kill us when they find out
we lied about going night fishing.

292
00:32:48.189 --> 00:32:49.481
How would they find out?

293
00:32:50.231 --> 00:32:51.522
We go every week.

294
00:32:54.064 --> 00:32:56.356
-How is it, Alex?
-We need to get closer.

295
00:33:20.481 --> 00:33:21.939
Let's get out of here.

296
00:33:24.647 --> 00:33:25.647
Shoot.

297
00:33:49.731 --> 00:33:51.106
Wait for me!

298
00:33:58.814 --> 00:34:01.064
Wait for me! Damn it!

299
00:34:03.897 --> 00:34:05.356
Wait for me!

300
00:34:10.981 --> 00:34:12.439
Wait!

301
00:34:39.272 --> 00:34:40.564
It's no use.

302
00:34:44.731 --> 00:34:48.022
-Why are you all up at 5:00 a.m.?
-They took all our men away.

303
00:34:48.106 --> 00:34:50.897
-And where were you? Out boozing?
-What happened?

304
00:34:50.981 --> 00:34:54.189
-There's a fire at the station.
-And they disconnected the phones.

305
00:34:56.356 --> 00:34:59.647
Damn it. Just when I got
a transfer out of here…

306
00:36:23.939 --> 00:36:26.272
Stop!

307
00:36:29.022 --> 00:36:31.606
Guys, I need a lift. I'm a fireman.

308
00:36:31.689 --> 00:36:32.981
Got a spare uniform for me?

309
00:36:45.147 --> 00:36:46.939
Hey, brother, is that the reactor?

310
00:36:47.564 --> 00:36:49.731
The pride and joy of the Soviet Union.

311
00:36:49.814 --> 00:36:52.814
Are you from around here?
Do you know why the forest has gone brown?

312
00:37:47.939 --> 00:37:51.022
-Move it!
-Go!

313
00:37:54.439 --> 00:37:56.481
Sir, I need to join my team!

314
00:37:56.564 --> 00:37:57.981
-Are you local?
-Yes, sir.

315
00:37:58.064 --> 00:37:59.939
I think your guys
are over on the other side.

316
00:38:00.022 --> 00:38:00.981
Come on!

317
00:38:02.981 --> 00:38:06.731
Get one more hose over there! Hurry!

318
00:38:16.522 --> 00:38:17.606
Tigran?

319
00:38:17.689 --> 00:38:19.647
Pour the water here!

320
00:38:19.731 --> 00:38:20.564
Tigran?

321
00:38:23.189 --> 00:38:24.606
Tigran?

322
00:38:24.689 --> 00:38:27.481
Tigran… where are our guys?

323
00:38:28.439 --> 00:38:30.106
They're over there.

324
00:38:31.606 --> 00:38:34.481
We were here first. The fire's over there.

325
00:38:38.106 --> 00:38:39.897
More water!

326
00:38:40.856 --> 00:38:42.689
Why are you not with the others?

327
00:38:42.772 --> 00:38:45.856
They told me to go up on the roof.

328
00:38:45.939 --> 00:38:47.522
The light was something unreal.

329
00:38:47.606 --> 00:38:51.606
I looked right into it.
It's unreal, like it's alive.

330
00:38:53.772 --> 00:38:55.106
You're not making any sense.

331
00:38:56.564 --> 00:38:58.189
The reactor exploded.

332
00:39:01.731 --> 00:39:04.022
Are you crazy? How could it explode?

333
00:39:23.814 --> 00:39:25.356
Tigran.

334
00:39:28.856 --> 00:39:30.772
Hang on, buddy.

335
00:39:33.147 --> 00:39:36.356
Over here! Hurry!

336
00:39:39.772 --> 00:39:42.689
-We have a severe case!
-Over here!

337
00:39:52.731 --> 00:39:54.606
Iodine thyroid block, now!

338
00:40:18.064 --> 00:40:21.147
-Careful.
-And lift.

339
00:40:21.231 --> 00:40:23.064
Into the ambulance, quick!

340
00:40:38.064 --> 00:40:39.314
Yuri!

341
00:40:41.147 --> 00:40:42.189
Get down here!

342
00:41:06.189 --> 00:41:09.231
Hang on, buddy.

343
00:41:09.939 --> 00:41:10.981
Lie still.

344
00:41:14.189 --> 00:41:15.272
PRIPYAT

345
00:41:17.439 --> 00:41:21.064
Don't get up. Help's on its way.

346
00:41:21.147 --> 00:41:23.897
-Yuri, get down here!
-Sergey!

347
00:41:24.731 --> 00:41:27.106
Alex, we've got to go up.

348
00:41:27.772 --> 00:41:29.772
Yuri's still on the roof.
Let's go get him.

349
00:41:33.397 --> 00:41:36.939
Hey, give me your breather.

350
00:41:59.397 --> 00:42:00.272
Sergey, you okay?

351
00:42:02.064 --> 00:42:04.356
Up there, the bitumen's on fire.

352
00:42:10.147 --> 00:42:12.397
Stay here. I'll be back in a minute.

353
00:42:45.064 --> 00:42:47.772
Yuri! Where are you? Yuri!

354
00:42:58.481 --> 00:43:00.981
Yuri. Get up.

355
00:43:03.981 --> 00:43:05.439
My face is all burned, right?

356
00:43:10.231 --> 00:43:13.272
Get up. Come on, get up!

357
00:43:15.772 --> 00:43:21.106
I got you. Now let's get out
of here. Come on. Let's go.

358
00:43:27.814 --> 00:43:29.272
Come on, get up.

359
00:43:52.147 --> 00:43:53.606
Come on.

360
00:43:53.689 --> 00:43:56.189
Sergey, you okay?

361
00:43:58.231 --> 00:44:00.731
I'm fine.

362
00:44:01.522 --> 00:44:02.439
You two go.

363
00:44:27.481 --> 00:44:29.981
Medic! Now!

364
00:44:51.522 --> 00:44:57.647
Sergey, I'm here. Come on, get up.

365
00:44:57.731 --> 00:45:01.147
Breathe, Sergey, breathe!

366
00:45:03.772 --> 00:45:06.022
Over here! Hurry!

367
00:45:10.231 --> 00:45:13.356
Boys, we have orders
to extract all the severe cases!

368
00:45:13.439 --> 00:45:14.647
Who's been vomiting?

369
00:45:15.814 --> 00:45:18.439
We picked men up from the third entrance--

370
00:45:18.522 --> 00:45:20.606
Load them in! You get in.

371
00:45:20.689 --> 00:45:23.397
Third entrance. Lots of them.

372
00:45:24.397 --> 00:45:26.772
I have to get them to hospital.

373
00:45:26.856 --> 00:45:29.106
Luda, hurry up.

374
00:45:29.189 --> 00:45:33.897
Luda, hurry up, I have to get them
to hospital. There are more, a lot more.

375
00:45:34.606 --> 00:45:36.731
-Take me with you.
-No, we're full!

376
00:45:36.814 --> 00:45:39.439
-They are my guys.
-There's no room!

377
00:45:39.522 --> 00:45:41.814
Please take me with you.

378
00:45:42.397 --> 00:45:44.856
I have my orders,
only severe cases. Let's go!

379
00:45:44.939 --> 00:45:47.272
-Need to get them to the hospital--
-Start the engine!

380
00:45:47.356 --> 00:45:49.147
Take me with you.

381
00:45:50.439 --> 00:45:51.856
Start the engine!

382
00:46:02.939 --> 00:46:04.814
-Can you drive? Let's go!
-Yes.

383
00:46:07.981 --> 00:46:09.439
-But--
-Move over!

384
00:46:36.064 --> 00:46:37.231
He's not breathing.

385
00:46:39.481 --> 00:46:41.106
Keep going! Don't stop!

386
00:46:46.356 --> 00:46:47.814
Everything's completely swollen up.

387
00:46:52.689 --> 00:46:54.064
Hold his head straight.

388
00:47:08.564 --> 00:47:09.897
Keep it steady!

389
00:47:34.022 --> 00:47:35.397
How is he?

390
00:47:37.189 --> 00:47:38.356
He's breathing.

391
00:47:40.189 --> 00:47:42.231
Go. Go!

392
00:47:49.606 --> 00:47:51.022
Careful!

393
00:47:57.606 --> 00:47:58.856
Get up.

394
00:48:08.897 --> 00:48:10.522
Put him in ward three!

395
00:48:14.647 --> 00:48:16.481
-Where to?
-Ward three is full.

396
00:48:24.564 --> 00:48:26.022
Don't just stand there. Move on.

397
00:48:36.439 --> 00:48:38.022
Kristina, get supplies ready.

398
00:48:38.106 --> 00:48:39.981
-Give this one a shot.
-Take your clothes off.

399
00:48:43.147 --> 00:48:44.897
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

400
00:49:19.481 --> 00:49:21.272
Kristina, diazepam.

401
00:49:21.356 --> 00:49:24.231
-What's that?
-A sedative to calm you down.

402
00:49:24.314 --> 00:49:27.022
-Put him in ward two.
-It's full.

403
00:49:27.106 --> 00:49:28.814
-Ward four then.
-No space there, either.

404
00:49:28.897 --> 00:49:30.731
There's one now,
Shinkarenko didn't make it.

405
00:49:31.731 --> 00:49:33.189
They just took him out.

406
00:49:50.397 --> 00:49:51.439
This way.

407
00:49:55.481 --> 00:49:56.731
Hurry up with the sheets.

408
00:49:58.231 --> 00:49:59.772
Go, I'll finish here.

409
00:50:00.647 --> 00:50:01.772
Lie down.

410
00:50:36.231 --> 00:50:39.522
Alexey, wake up.

411
00:50:42.772 --> 00:50:43.981
Alexey, wake up.

412
00:50:44.731 --> 00:50:45.731
Alexey?

413
00:50:46.481 --> 00:50:48.314
Get up. Are you Alexey Karpushin?

414
00:50:51.189 --> 00:50:52.022
Yes.

415
00:50:52.647 --> 00:50:54.022
How long was I asleep?

416
00:50:54.106 --> 00:50:56.064
Quite a while.
They overdid it with the sedative.

417
00:51:00.397 --> 00:51:01.481
Do you feel nauseous?

418
00:51:04.231 --> 00:51:06.272
-I don't think so.
-Are you feeling okay?

419
00:51:09.439 --> 00:51:10.272
Yes.

420
00:51:18.147 --> 00:51:19.981
Good. Very well then.

421
00:51:21.272 --> 00:51:24.022
Alexey, my name is Dina,
I'm a radiologist from Kiev.

422
00:51:24.106 --> 00:51:26.814
We came here to see you.
They'll bring you new clothes.

423
00:51:26.897 --> 00:51:29.522
I'll wait in the corridor
while you get dressed.

424
00:51:42.314 --> 00:51:43.939
-Nikolai?
-Go away.

425
00:51:44.939 --> 00:51:45.856
Go away!

426
00:51:47.606 --> 00:51:50.022
Nikolai!

427
00:51:50.981 --> 00:51:52.272
Nikolai!

428
00:51:57.231 --> 00:52:00.064
-Go away, go home!
-Please step away from the window.

429
00:52:00.814 --> 00:52:02.272
You could get us in trouble.

430
00:52:03.731 --> 00:52:05.731
Alexey Prihodko?

431
00:52:09.064 --> 00:52:11.147
-Why can't they come in?
-You're contaminated.

432
00:52:11.231 --> 00:52:12.481
What are we contaminated with?

433
00:52:16.481 --> 00:52:18.897
Radiation. You all
react differently to it.

434
00:52:18.981 --> 00:52:20.981
Some die after five minutes of exposure.

435
00:52:21.064 --> 00:52:23.147
Some are fine after five hours.

436
00:52:24.147 --> 00:52:25.897
You got lucky, you only got 14 rem.

437
00:52:34.106 --> 00:52:36.147
All the contaminated clothes
go into the basement.

438
00:52:36.231 --> 00:52:39.856
All of you who just arrived,
leave your clothes by the entrance!

439
00:52:41.481 --> 00:52:43.981
-Here's Karpushin.
-Hold on a minute.

440
00:52:45.439 --> 00:52:46.814
Are you Alexey Karpushin?

441
00:52:47.522 --> 00:52:48.647
Yes, hello.

442
00:52:48.731 --> 00:52:51.647
-From the reactor fire service?
-Chief of watch, sixth brigade.

443
00:52:51.731 --> 00:52:54.231
-Do you know the corridors below?
-Like the back of my hand.

444
00:52:54.314 --> 00:52:55.814
Have you ever scuba dived?

445
00:52:56.397 --> 00:52:57.606
No, only snorkeled.

446
00:52:58.231 --> 00:53:00.897
I see. You're coming with us.

447
00:53:00.981 --> 00:53:03.439
Look, I left the service here
and got a transfer to Kiev.

448
00:53:06.231 --> 00:53:10.189
You're coming with us,
and we'll discuss your transfer later.

449
00:53:10.272 --> 00:53:12.439
Close the door and wait.
I'll be with you shortly.

450
00:53:14.731 --> 00:53:16.106
Doctor, you can stay.

451
00:53:18.356 --> 00:53:19.481
Yes, hello?

452
00:53:52.106 --> 00:53:53.481
The kids are all outdoors.

453
00:54:14.147 --> 00:54:17.022
Comrade Stysin, we can start now.

454
00:54:17.106 --> 00:54:19.606
Hello, Comrade Karpushin.
I'm Mikhail, this is Ivan.

455
00:54:19.689 --> 00:54:22.397
We're with a government commission
responding to the incident.

456
00:54:22.481 --> 00:54:24.522
Hi, Valery. Any news about Sergey?

457
00:54:24.606 --> 00:54:26.689
They took him to Kiev, he's in bad shape.

458
00:54:28.939 --> 00:54:31.814
Comrades, I apologize for
bringing you all here with no explanation.

459
00:54:31.897 --> 00:54:34.189
I shall explain now.
Ivan, please turn on the video.

460
00:54:48.147 --> 00:54:51.939
Between the third and fourth units
is the crater left by the explosion.

461
00:54:52.022 --> 00:54:54.439
The reactor core
is in a sub-critical condition.

462
00:54:54.522 --> 00:54:57.522
All these bright spots
are clumps of burning reactor fuel.

463
00:54:58.189 --> 00:55:00.231
Temperatures could increase to the point

464
00:55:00.314 --> 00:55:03.564
where it melts through the floor
of the reactor and the concrete below.

465
00:55:04.522 --> 00:55:08.772
The coolant water reservoirs
are directly underneath the reactor.

466
00:55:09.647 --> 00:55:13.481
As you know, if enough fuel
burns through and gets to the water,

467
00:55:13.564 --> 00:55:15.189
there will be a steam explosion…

468
00:55:15.772 --> 00:55:18.606
that will cause
further ejection of radioactive material.

469
00:55:21.356 --> 00:55:23.481
If the core reaches the reservoirs,

470
00:55:23.564 --> 00:55:27.564
Kiev, Moscow… and the whole
of Europe will be contaminated.

471
00:55:34.147 --> 00:55:36.314
So we must get the water out of there.

472
00:55:38.064 --> 00:55:39.981
Your departments have staff

473
00:55:40.064 --> 00:55:42.772
who are familiar with
the corridors beneath the reactor.

474
00:55:42.856 --> 00:55:46.522
Comrade Kostenko, water management.
Comrade Maksimov, electrical service.

475
00:55:46.606 --> 00:55:50.064
Valery Goncharuk, cooling systems,
and Comrade Karpushin, fire service.

476
00:55:50.147 --> 00:55:52.647
Colonel Bobylin
will be assisting with the operation.

477
00:55:58.189 --> 00:56:00.647
We need you
to recommend staff from your departments

478
00:56:00.731 --> 00:56:04.356
who know the corridors under the reactor
well enough to open the sluice gates.

479
00:56:05.647 --> 00:56:07.397
How do you intend to do that

480
00:56:07.481 --> 00:56:09.981
if the water management block
is destroyed?

481
00:56:10.064 --> 00:56:12.064
The control panel is under rubble.

482
00:56:13.272 --> 00:56:15.356
We can go through
the pipe conduit corridor

483
00:56:15.439 --> 00:56:17.564
and open the drainage valve manually.

484
00:56:27.356 --> 00:56:29.189
But it's all flooded with hot water.

485
00:56:30.772 --> 00:56:34.939
People will be working in diving gear,
and get diving instruction beforehand.

486
00:56:36.356 --> 00:56:39.647
If the servo is flooded, it'll take half
an hour to open the valve by hand.

487
00:56:39.731 --> 00:56:43.397
Two people working together can do it
in under eight minutes, we were assured.

488
00:56:43.481 --> 00:56:48.397
You want us to volunteer our own people
and send them to boil for eight minutes?

489
00:56:50.522 --> 00:56:53.147
The volunteers will be rewarded.

490
00:56:53.981 --> 00:56:58.314
We're also getting a plane ready
to take them to Switzerland for treatment

491
00:56:58.439 --> 00:57:01.106
in a specialist radiation clinic.

492
00:57:01.189 --> 00:57:02.772
The most outstanding volunteers

493
00:57:02.856 --> 00:57:05.106
will be awarded
private apartments in Moscow.

494
00:57:05.689 --> 00:57:08.814
The General Secretary
will see to it personally.

495
00:57:09.772 --> 00:57:10.731
Isn't that enough?

496
00:57:50.314 --> 00:57:52.314
Well, if the servo motor isn't flooded,

497
00:57:52.397 --> 00:57:54.189
can we power it up directly?

498
00:57:58.314 --> 00:58:01.897
You'll need the nearest junction box,
in case there are breaks in the cables.

499
00:58:02.689 --> 00:58:05.522
One closest to the motor is here.
I don't know how to get to it.

500
00:58:05.606 --> 00:58:08.231
We only go down there
once a year, with guides.

501
00:58:08.314 --> 00:58:09.981
Ivan, where's the map of the corridors?

502
00:58:14.814 --> 00:58:18.064
This is what we know about
the radiation levels down there.

503
00:58:18.147 --> 00:58:21.481
The levels
in the corridors on the western side

504
00:58:21.564 --> 00:58:23.856
are lower than in the conduit corridors,

505
00:58:24.439 --> 00:58:26.564
and there should be less water.

506
00:58:26.647 --> 00:58:28.981
There are too many unknowns.

507
00:58:29.064 --> 00:58:30.647
What if the servo is flooded?

508
00:58:30.731 --> 00:58:34.356
So, you'd rather send inexperienced
divers to work in murky water?

509
00:58:35.272 --> 00:58:37.106
Can you guarantee
that your plan will work?

510
00:58:39.731 --> 00:58:40.564
No.

511
00:58:40.647 --> 00:58:43.689
But everyone
who stays down there long enough

512
00:58:44.397 --> 00:58:46.022
is guaranteed to be exposed.

513
00:58:46.106 --> 00:58:47.814
We won't stay long down there.

514
00:58:47.897 --> 00:58:49.856
The water temperature is 56C, bearable.

515
00:58:49.939 --> 00:58:52.564
And we only have 100 meters to go.

516
00:58:52.647 --> 00:58:54.189
Give us people who can show us

517
00:58:54.272 --> 00:58:56.731
what valves to turn,
then they can go straight back out.

518
00:58:58.564 --> 00:59:00.606
It'd be safest to go via Level 7.

519
00:59:01.189 --> 00:59:03.981
By the time we're done
wandering around this labyrinth,

520
00:59:04.064 --> 00:59:09.272
the water temperature will hit 70C,
and no one will go swimming in that.

521
00:59:17.897 --> 00:59:19.897
Comrade Stysin,
can we go and see the pool now?

522
00:59:19.981 --> 00:59:22.939
Yes, of course. Let's go.

523
00:59:37.481 --> 00:59:38.897
Nikita, let's hear it.

524
00:59:38.981 --> 00:59:42.939
We stayed under for 12 minutes,
but the temperature right now is only 51C.

525
00:59:43.022 --> 00:59:45.106
We'll now increase it to 56C.

526
00:59:45.189 --> 00:59:47.814
As you were. As you can see,
we're preparing thoroughly.

527
00:59:47.897 --> 00:59:51.939
But without your help,
we won't know which valve to open.

528
00:59:52.022 --> 00:59:54.856
There are miles of pipes in murky water.

529
00:59:54.939 --> 00:59:56.481
We won't have a clue what to do.

530
00:59:56.564 --> 00:59:58.189
Have you ever dived in hot water before?

531
01:00:00.022 --> 01:00:02.064
We know about extreme temperatures.

532
01:00:02.147 --> 01:00:04.147
We're talking hot, dirty water
in a confined space,

533
01:00:04.231 --> 01:00:05.606
not in a clean swimming pool.

534
01:00:05.689 --> 01:00:07.731
Engineers aren't trained
for such conditions.

535
01:00:09.189 --> 01:00:11.731
We'll train them here… in the pool.

536
01:00:12.606 --> 01:00:14.981
You'll give your own guys
hyperthermia right here,

537
01:00:15.064 --> 01:00:17.106
and none of them
will even make it to the reactor.

538
01:00:20.189 --> 01:00:23.356
I can't order my people
to do something like this.

539
01:00:23.439 --> 01:00:24.522
They're not soldiers.

540
01:00:25.272 --> 01:00:28.397
Comrades, this is not
a question of can or can't.

541
01:00:29.814 --> 01:00:32.981
It is a question of do or die.

542
01:00:45.606 --> 01:00:48.856
I'm sorry, but my men
don't know those corridors well enough.

543
01:00:48.939 --> 01:00:51.772
No electricity in the station,
not enough people, like you said.

544
01:00:55.564 --> 01:00:59.231
I can't order my men to do this either.

545
01:01:01.606 --> 01:01:03.356
If you decide to go in at Level 7…

546
01:01:05.731 --> 01:01:06.814
I'll go myself.

547
01:01:09.189 --> 01:01:10.356
Me too.

548
01:01:18.022 --> 01:01:21.606
Boris… we'll go in at Level 7.

549
01:01:22.981 --> 01:01:25.272
We have no right
to risk these people's lives.

550
01:01:33.064 --> 01:01:35.897
Do we have the right
to risk the lives of people in Kiev

551
01:01:35.981 --> 01:01:38.481
who are getting ready
for the May Day parade?

552
01:01:45.689 --> 01:01:46.689
Fine.

553
01:01:48.356 --> 01:01:52.314
Try going in… at Level 7.

554
01:02:06.231 --> 01:02:08.189
Do we have
the support of the fire service?

555
01:02:09.981 --> 01:02:13.564
I don't work here as of yesterday.
I don't have any authority to give orders.

556
01:02:14.647 --> 01:02:17.689
In any case, almost
the entire local brigade is hospitalized.

557
01:02:20.397 --> 01:02:21.481
I won't go in there.

558
01:02:27.356 --> 01:02:33.356
Didn't you give an oath to protect
your country with your own life?

559
01:02:42.481 --> 01:02:44.897
Fine, let's decide on the route.

560
01:03:09.522 --> 01:03:14.147
Attention, everyone.

561
01:03:14.231 --> 01:03:16.772
Dear comrades,

562
01:03:16.856 --> 01:03:21.522
the City Council
of People's Deputies informs you that,

563
01:03:21.606 --> 01:03:24.106
due to an incident

564
01:03:24.189 --> 01:03:29.231
at the Chernobyl Nuclear Power Plant,

565
01:03:29.314 --> 01:03:32.439
there is an adverse radioactive situation

566
01:03:32.522 --> 01:03:35.522
in the town of Pripyat.

567
01:03:35.606 --> 01:03:39.356
Authorities and the military

568
01:03:39.439 --> 01:03:44.231
are taking all necessary measures.

569
01:03:44.981 --> 01:03:50.772
Nonetheless, in order
to ensure safety of the townspeople,

570
01:03:50.856 --> 01:03:54.022
children being top priority,

571
01:03:54.106 --> 01:03:58.606
we need to temporarily evacuate civilians…

572
01:04:01.731 --> 01:04:04.314
Olga!

573
01:04:06.981 --> 01:04:08.397
-Olga!
-Alex got very sick.

574
01:04:09.064 --> 01:04:10.772
-Hey there, Jackie Chan.
-Hi.

575
01:04:12.939 --> 01:04:14.231
What's wrong with him?

576
01:04:14.314 --> 01:04:17.231
Same as with everyone.
I don't know. We have to get out of here.

577
01:04:20.064 --> 01:04:21.397
Have the doctors seen him?

578
01:04:21.981 --> 01:04:25.314
No. The hospital is packed full
of sick kids, all screaming and crying.

579
01:04:26.022 --> 01:04:27.689
There's talk of a wave of miscarriages.

580
01:04:27.772 --> 01:04:29.231
Miscarriages, understand?

581
01:04:29.772 --> 01:04:31.897
The police have cordoned off the hospital.

582
01:04:36.439 --> 01:04:38.647
Hey, how are you feeling?

583
01:04:39.606 --> 01:04:41.897
I saw the explosion and then a glow.

584
01:04:42.897 --> 01:04:44.189
Did anyone get killed?

585
01:04:44.272 --> 01:04:46.731
No, it was just an ordinary fire--

586
01:04:46.814 --> 01:04:47.939
Are you my dad?

587
01:04:53.356 --> 01:04:54.981
No. Why do you ask?

588
01:05:07.356 --> 01:05:08.814
Did Mom tell you that?

589
01:05:09.564 --> 01:05:12.356
We'll talk about this later.
We need to go now.

590
01:05:13.606 --> 01:05:14.772
Come on, get up.

591
01:05:14.856 --> 01:05:16.231
You're not a little kid.

592
01:05:16.314 --> 01:05:18.522
I'm not going anywhere.

593
01:05:18.606 --> 01:05:19.689
We have to go.

594
01:05:20.314 --> 01:05:21.439
Come on.

595
01:05:21.522 --> 01:05:23.314
We're never coming back here, right?

596
01:05:23.397 --> 01:05:25.397
Of course, we'll come back.

597
01:05:26.856 --> 01:05:29.231
You're lying!

598
01:05:29.314 --> 01:05:30.647
-Grab our bag.
-I want my camera!

599
01:05:31.897 --> 01:05:36.022
I'm not going anywhere! I don't want to!

600
01:05:36.814 --> 01:05:37.981
I'm not going!

601
01:05:47.772 --> 01:05:48.731
Olga, let me help.

602
01:05:51.647 --> 01:05:53.147
No animals allowed.

603
01:05:53.231 --> 01:05:56.981
-You can't take animals with you.
-But it's my dog! Dad, tell him!

604
01:05:57.939 --> 01:06:00.189
Sweetie, we'll come back for him later.

605
01:06:01.147 --> 01:06:03.356
-Give me the key.
-Don't lock him inside.

606
01:06:03.439 --> 01:06:05.731
-We have a sick child.
-The doctors are over there.

607
01:06:05.814 --> 01:06:06.939
Olga, follow me.

608
01:06:09.106 --> 01:06:10.439
Come.

609
01:06:14.647 --> 01:06:16.147
-Olga, over here.
-Alex…

610
01:06:23.231 --> 01:06:25.272
Olga, there's an ambulance.

611
01:06:29.606 --> 01:06:31.814
Sorry, it's an emergency.

612
01:06:31.897 --> 01:06:34.356
-My child is sick, please help.
-Let's see his throat.

613
01:06:36.356 --> 01:06:38.814
-Has he been vomiting?
-He vomited yesterday.

614
01:06:38.897 --> 01:06:42.272
Everyone with radiation sickness
must go to Hospital No. 6 in Kiev.

615
01:06:42.356 --> 01:06:44.356
He can't even stand. We need an ambulance.

616
01:06:44.439 --> 01:06:46.356
You'll have to discuss that in Kiev.

617
01:06:46.439 --> 01:06:48.064
He can hardly breathe!

618
01:06:48.147 --> 01:06:49.981
What's your name, please?

619
01:06:52.856 --> 01:06:54.814
Olga Savostina. My son is Alexey Savostin.

620
01:06:57.564 --> 01:06:59.231
-Can I talk to you?
-Hands off me.

621
01:06:59.314 --> 01:07:00.397
Just for a second.

622
01:07:00.481 --> 01:07:02.772
Hands off me.
Can't you see what's going on here?

623
01:07:02.856 --> 01:07:06.189
Everyone's leaving town on buses.
I don't make decisions here. Name?

624
01:07:07.481 --> 01:07:08.314
Alexey Savostin.

625
01:07:08.897 --> 01:07:09.772
Savostin.

626
01:07:09.856 --> 01:07:10.814
Get on the bus.

627
01:07:11.439 --> 01:07:12.272
Let's go.

628
01:07:56.814 --> 01:07:59.356
Mom, I want out of the bus.

629
01:07:59.939 --> 01:08:01.564
Hang in there, sweetie.

630
01:08:02.356 --> 01:08:05.397
-Mom…
-Everything will be fine.

631
01:08:12.231 --> 01:08:16.231
Oh, God, what's happening?

632
01:08:17.814 --> 01:08:22.356
We'll be in Kiev soon,
we'll get help there. Don't worry.

633
01:08:22.439 --> 01:08:23.272
Stop it.

634
01:08:24.022 --> 01:08:25.481
Stop promising.

635
01:08:26.314 --> 01:08:27.397
Who's going to help us?

636
01:08:27.481 --> 01:08:29.564
They're transporting us
like cattle. Stop lying!

637
01:08:31.564 --> 01:08:33.356
I'm not lying. I'm trying to help.

638
01:08:34.522 --> 01:08:37.981
-I owe you that much.
-You don't owe us anything. Nothing!

639
01:08:38.064 --> 01:08:41.272
Mom, why are you yelling at him?

640
01:08:44.064 --> 01:08:46.856
I'm sorry.

641
01:08:50.106 --> 01:08:51.856
I just can't take it anymore.

642
01:09:18.147 --> 01:09:19.856
Take this, it's almost 300 rubles.

643
01:09:20.522 --> 01:09:22.522
I'll arrange
the best treatment there is for Alex,

644
01:09:22.606 --> 01:09:24.231
but now I have to go back.

645
01:09:27.981 --> 01:09:30.689
Hang in there, buddy.
You'll be good as new in no time.

646
01:10:46.439 --> 01:10:47.272
You in charge here?

647
01:10:47.356 --> 01:10:49.689
This man says he wants to volunteer,

648
01:10:49.772 --> 01:10:51.356
something about pumping water.

649
01:10:51.439 --> 01:10:54.147
-Alexey Karpushin, fire service.
-I know you, I was at the meeting.

650
01:10:54.231 --> 01:10:55.189
I want to volunteer.

651
01:10:57.564 --> 01:10:58.981
Oleg, talk to Frolov for me.

652
01:11:01.147 --> 01:11:03.231
Thanks, Captain, we'll take it from here.

653
01:11:03.314 --> 01:11:06.647
You just missed them, they went off
to the third reactor to check the route.

654
01:11:06.731 --> 01:11:09.147
You can go with the second group

655
01:11:09.231 --> 01:11:11.064
if the first group fails.

656
01:11:11.147 --> 01:11:12.731
How can I join the first group?

657
01:11:13.397 --> 01:11:16.689
-Comrade Stysin calls shots here.
-I know the corridors better than anyone.

658
01:11:16.772 --> 01:11:19.897
All right. Wait for them here.
They'll be back in a couple of hours.

659
01:11:19.981 --> 01:11:21.314
Can I join them there now?

660
01:11:22.064 --> 01:11:23.439
They'll be back soon.

661
01:11:25.481 --> 01:11:27.981
-Show me the route they decided on.
-On the board.

662
01:11:28.064 --> 01:11:29.272
-This one?
-Yes.

663
01:11:29.356 --> 01:11:32.856
I can't understand these blueprints.
Do you have a fire evacuation diagram?

664
01:11:33.981 --> 01:11:35.147
To the left.

665
01:11:42.606 --> 01:11:44.272
-Like that, through Level 7?
-Yes.

666
01:11:46.689 --> 01:11:50.106
We can cut through here, it's closer.

667
01:11:51.981 --> 01:11:55.022
-Cut through reinforced concrete?
-There used to be a flight of stairs.

668
01:11:55.106 --> 01:11:57.939
They took it out
and covered the hole with a metal sheet.

669
01:11:58.022 --> 01:11:58.897
Where?

670
01:12:00.397 --> 01:12:01.856
-Here?
-Yes.

671
01:12:01.939 --> 01:12:03.272
Why didn't they mention it?

672
01:12:03.356 --> 01:12:06.272
They've been here since the launch,
but I saw the plant being built.

673
01:12:06.356 --> 01:12:08.606
Take me there,
I'll show you the shortest way.

674
01:12:09.856 --> 01:12:12.397
Marchenko… get us a helicopter.

675
01:13:30.731 --> 01:13:33.022
Comrade Stysin, there's a shorter route.

676
01:13:33.106 --> 01:13:33.939
Show us.

677
01:13:34.022 --> 01:13:35.439
-Hi, Valery.
-Hi.

678
01:13:42.439 --> 01:13:43.272
Here it is.

679
01:13:43.939 --> 01:13:47.106
We can cut through it
and shorten the route.

680
01:13:50.439 --> 01:13:53.647
I did the calculations already,
this route is 150 meters shorter.

681
01:13:54.606 --> 01:13:56.314
Why isn't this in the blueprints?

682
01:13:56.397 --> 01:13:58.314
The blueprints
are verified, but in reality,

683
01:13:58.397 --> 01:14:00.481
a lot of things were built differently

684
01:14:00.564 --> 01:14:01.856
to meet deadlines.

685
01:14:02.731 --> 01:14:04.064
Good news for us, though.

686
01:14:04.147 --> 01:14:07.272
Comrade Stysin,
we won't be taking the fireman with us.

687
01:14:07.356 --> 01:14:12.272
We appreciate the tour, but down there
in the dark, we'll need reliable people.

688
01:14:20.022 --> 01:14:21.689
You'll come with the first group.

689
01:14:25.106 --> 01:14:28.314
-Are you doing this for the reward?
-What are you doing this for?

690
01:14:30.606 --> 01:14:32.189
I'm doing my duty.

691
01:14:41.064 --> 01:14:44.147
Are you Olga Savostina?
You have a phone call from Pripyat.

692
01:15:01.606 --> 01:15:02.647
-Hello?
-Olga…

693
01:15:03.356 --> 01:15:05.772
I found you at last. How are things?

694
01:15:05.856 --> 01:15:09.481
I don't know. They took Alex away.
They're not telling me how he is.

695
01:15:09.564 --> 01:15:10.481
He'll be fine.

696
01:15:10.564 --> 01:15:13.106
I'm making arrangements
for the best treatment for him,

697
01:15:13.189 --> 01:15:15.481
and then we'll all go live by the sea.

698
01:15:17.106 --> 01:15:19.606
-Olga?
-I can't talk to you anymore.

699
01:15:19.689 --> 01:15:22.397
-Olga? Hello?
-I'm sorry, I just can't.

700
01:15:22.481 --> 01:15:23.856
Olga, hello?

701
01:15:35.731 --> 01:15:38.647
-Comrade Stysin, I have a favor to ask.
-Go ahead.

702
01:15:40.064 --> 01:15:41.689
My son was exposed to radiation.

703
01:15:42.314 --> 01:15:44.439
Can he go to Switzerland, too?

704
01:15:47.522 --> 01:15:48.522
Comrade Tropin.

705
01:15:49.606 --> 01:15:54.022
Alexey has some conditions he'd like
to discuss before going under the reactor.

706
01:15:55.772 --> 01:15:59.272
-What conditions?
-No conditions, just a favor to ask.

707
01:16:02.856 --> 01:16:05.147
My son was near
the reactor when it exploded.

708
01:16:06.731 --> 01:16:09.772
Would it be possible for him to go
to Switzerland for treatment, too?

709
01:16:10.606 --> 01:16:14.522
The passenger list will be
confirmed by the General Secretary,

710
01:16:14.606 --> 01:16:16.522
and only liquidators are on it.

711
01:16:16.606 --> 01:16:19.522
Surely, it's easier for him
to add a name to a list

712
01:16:19.606 --> 01:16:21.814
than to evacuate the whole of Kiev?

713
01:16:22.856 --> 01:16:26.897
You don't quite understand
how the bureaucratic machine works.

714
01:16:27.647 --> 01:16:29.814
Then can he go instead of me?

715
01:16:30.314 --> 01:16:34.022
And you can send me to a hospital
in Moscow or Kiev. Could that be done?

716
01:16:35.981 --> 01:16:38.147
I think we can arrange for that.

717
01:16:40.522 --> 01:16:41.897
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

718
01:16:41.981 --> 01:16:44.106
Would you mind
showing me your credentials?

719
01:16:45.272 --> 01:16:46.522
So that I can be sure.

720
01:16:58.647 --> 01:17:00.022
I'm convinced.

721
01:17:02.314 --> 01:17:03.397
You should be.

722
01:17:13.522 --> 01:17:14.731
Here are your masks.

723
01:17:14.814 --> 01:17:17.397
The water shouldn't be deep,
but take them just in case.

724
01:17:18.314 --> 01:17:21.231
If you run into
a field of radiation, go around it.

725
01:17:21.314 --> 01:17:23.647
-We'll manage.
-Ivan, let's hear the drill again.

726
01:17:23.731 --> 01:17:25.772
You get to mark 01, cut through the floor

727
01:17:25.856 --> 01:17:28.356
and go along DU-1
to the junction box that powers the servo.

728
01:17:28.439 --> 01:17:30.231
You hook up the cable and wait.

729
01:17:30.314 --> 01:17:33.231
We'll power it up in exactly 20 minutes.
Let's synchronize watches.

730
01:17:36.022 --> 01:17:37.689
Alexey, I found out about Alex.

731
01:17:37.772 --> 01:17:40.022
The boy
was definitely exposed to radiation,

732
01:17:40.106 --> 01:17:43.606
but with treatment in Switzerland,
he should make a full recovery.

733
01:17:43.689 --> 01:17:44.814
Thank you.

734
01:17:44.897 --> 01:17:48.189
Just do what you have to do,
and we'll take care of the rest.

735
01:17:49.064 --> 01:17:51.564
-Time for you to go.
-Let's roll.

736
01:17:53.356 --> 01:17:54.897
Nikita, let's go.

737
01:18:28.481 --> 01:18:29.897
What force are you with?

738
01:18:31.147 --> 01:18:32.439
Foreign intelligence.

739
01:18:32.522 --> 01:18:35.647
Holy cow! Do we have
a lot of enemies out there?

740
01:18:37.897 --> 01:18:39.522
Your bosses are a bit harsh.

741
01:18:39.606 --> 01:18:41.439
They are okay. Keep hold of the reel.

742
01:18:42.647 --> 01:18:43.897
We're here.

743
01:18:45.814 --> 01:18:47.189
This is where we need to cut.

744
01:19:08.981 --> 01:19:09.814
How is it?

745
01:19:13.356 --> 01:19:14.356
Could be worse.

746
01:19:16.481 --> 01:19:18.481
Let's go. The stairs
are only two meters away.

747
01:20:08.481 --> 01:20:11.022
There can't be any steam
in the pipes after the accident.

748
01:20:11.106 --> 01:20:12.356
So, what's this then?

749
01:20:12.439 --> 01:20:15.772
Water must be getting in
somewhere from above and evaporating.

750
01:20:15.856 --> 01:20:17.647
The reactor is still hot as hell.

751
01:20:27.356 --> 01:20:29.314
Alex, let's close these valves!

752
01:20:29.397 --> 01:20:30.481
Okay.

753
01:20:32.106 --> 01:20:33.522
Nikita, go for it.

754
01:20:44.356 --> 01:20:45.689
Nikita, get away from there!

755
01:20:53.522 --> 01:20:54.606
Let's get him up.

756
01:20:56.356 --> 01:20:57.647
Sit him down.

757
01:21:04.189 --> 01:21:07.272
-You need to get out.
-I'll go on, Boris.

758
01:21:10.272 --> 01:21:12.356
No, wait for us here. We'll be quick.

759
01:21:12.981 --> 01:21:14.731
I'm fine to continue.

760
01:21:14.814 --> 01:21:18.064
Don't be stupid.
Wait here. We'll be back soon.

761
01:21:19.647 --> 01:21:21.522
Nikita, we'll be back soon.

762
01:21:25.564 --> 01:21:27.272
And lift.

763
01:21:48.022 --> 01:21:49.189
What's wrong, Valery?

764
01:21:53.189 --> 01:21:54.772
I'm not going any further.

765
01:22:25.647 --> 01:22:27.772
I'm sorry, I'm not going any further.

766
01:22:30.522 --> 01:22:32.439
But we can't do it without you.

767
01:22:32.522 --> 01:22:33.606
I can't go on.

768
01:22:38.147 --> 01:22:39.564
Let's talk, shall we?

769
01:22:43.772 --> 01:22:46.606
Get your breath back,
and then we'll have a little talk.

770
01:22:51.731 --> 01:22:53.772
I can't go on!

771
01:22:53.856 --> 01:22:56.731
My wife and kids in Kiev
are preparing to celebrate May Day,

772
01:22:56.814 --> 01:22:58.856
so stick your "can't go on" up your ass.

773
01:23:02.147 --> 01:23:03.939
-I'm sorry.
-Valery.

774
01:23:04.022 --> 01:23:05.897
-I'm sorry.
-You're having a panic attack.

775
01:23:05.981 --> 01:23:07.564
-Let go of me.
-Look me in the eyes.

776
01:23:07.647 --> 01:23:08.689
I said let go of me!

777
01:23:08.772 --> 01:23:12.856
-I'm not going!
-Look at me. Breathe with me.

778
01:23:12.939 --> 01:23:13.856
In and out.

779
01:23:13.939 --> 01:23:15.439
Come on, breathe.

780
01:23:16.814 --> 01:23:19.856
In and out.

781
01:23:20.564 --> 01:23:23.522
That's it, calm down.

782
01:23:28.814 --> 01:23:30.356
Do you think I'm not scared?

783
01:23:31.022 --> 01:23:33.981
Do you think Yuri Gagarin wasn't scared
when they shot him into space?

784
01:23:34.064 --> 01:23:35.939
He pissed himself inside that spacesuit.

785
01:23:38.064 --> 01:23:42.106
When we're done here, they'll take us
for a lap of honor around Red Square.

786
01:23:42.856 --> 01:23:44.897
Like they did with Korolev and Gagarin.

787
01:23:45.647 --> 01:23:47.481
You know how many women Gagarin had?

788
01:23:48.981 --> 01:23:51.397
-No.
-More than you, that's for sure.

789
01:23:54.772 --> 01:23:56.022
You're an idiot, Alex.

790
01:24:02.606 --> 01:24:04.731
Sergey died in Kiev of radiation sickness.

791
01:24:32.731 --> 01:24:35.022
Well, Valery,
I am not going to die just yet.

792
01:24:36.606 --> 01:24:41.189
I still have plans… and dreams.

793
01:24:44.022 --> 01:24:46.272
Do you think
I'm not scared of going in there?

794
01:24:58.397 --> 01:24:59.856
My legs won't move.

795
01:25:01.147 --> 01:25:02.689
Well, you just make them.

796
01:25:02.772 --> 01:25:05.397
Come on, up you go.

797
01:25:24.897 --> 01:25:26.231
It's like a sauna in here.

798
01:25:51.897 --> 01:25:53.314
-Crap!
-Is the cable in one piece?

799
01:25:53.397 --> 01:25:55.606
Looks like it, but the reel fell down.

800
01:26:01.231 --> 01:26:02.314
I feel dizzy.

801
01:26:02.397 --> 01:26:03.897
How many fingers am I holding up?

802
01:26:03.981 --> 01:26:06.106
Five. I think I might throw up.

803
01:26:24.272 --> 01:26:25.356
Help me out.

804
01:26:25.439 --> 01:26:26.731
I got you.

805
01:26:32.814 --> 01:26:34.564
Boris, it's scalding hot in there.

806
01:26:42.064 --> 01:26:43.189
You okay?

807
01:26:47.814 --> 01:26:48.939
We have six minutes.

808
01:26:49.897 --> 01:26:51.772
-Valery, get my flashlight.
-Okay.

809
01:26:53.731 --> 01:26:54.606
Give.

810
01:27:07.856 --> 01:27:09.314
There's the junction box.

811
01:27:14.314 --> 01:27:15.772
It's hot, but bearable.

812
01:27:15.856 --> 01:27:18.064
This water
makes you feel as if you're drunk.

813
01:27:23.439 --> 01:27:25.439
Boris, you stay here
and keep track of the time.

814
01:27:26.481 --> 01:27:28.481
I'll carry Valery
over to the junction box,

815
01:27:28.564 --> 01:27:30.314
and he'll hook the cable up.

816
01:27:31.064 --> 01:27:32.481
You remember the instructions?

817
01:27:33.022 --> 01:27:33.939
I do.

818
01:27:35.606 --> 01:27:36.856
Will you manage?

819
01:27:38.647 --> 01:27:39.481
Yes.

820
01:27:43.689 --> 01:27:44.564
Three minutes.

821
01:28:19.022 --> 01:28:20.272
Ninety seconds, Valery!

822
01:28:37.439 --> 01:28:39.314
Right. Disconnecting the breaker.

823
01:28:39.981 --> 01:28:40.897
Done.

824
01:28:43.314 --> 01:28:44.231
You okay?

825
01:28:45.022 --> 01:28:46.189
Yeah, keep at it.

826
01:28:51.647 --> 01:28:54.106
Connecting the cable
to the lower contacts of the breaker.

827
01:28:54.647 --> 01:28:55.981
One minute!

828
01:29:00.564 --> 01:29:01.856
One…

829
01:29:03.522 --> 01:29:04.772
and two.

830
01:29:08.189 --> 01:29:09.606
Connecting the breaker.

831
01:29:15.856 --> 01:29:17.272
Turning on the switch.

832
01:29:18.731 --> 01:29:21.272
-Thirty-two.
-I'm done, let's go back.

833
01:29:29.147 --> 01:29:31.147
Don't carry me, I'll walk.

834
01:29:34.439 --> 01:29:35.481
Come on.

835
01:30:00.481 --> 01:30:01.731
It worked!

836
01:30:02.564 --> 01:30:03.772
Holy crap!

837
01:30:05.397 --> 01:30:07.564
-We did it!
-Quiet.

838
01:30:07.647 --> 01:30:09.772
-The tester's lit up.
-Quiet. We should hear it.

839
01:30:13.606 --> 01:30:16.189
Yes! It worked!

840
01:30:17.022 --> 01:30:19.731
We did it! It worked!

841
01:30:20.439 --> 01:30:22.856
Comrade Colonel, it worked! We did it!

842
01:30:25.189 --> 01:30:26.439
We did it!

843
01:30:38.647 --> 01:30:41.814
It didn't work.
We'll have to open the valve by hand.

844
01:30:43.064 --> 01:30:44.564
Maybe we can try hotwiring it again?

845
01:30:44.647 --> 01:30:47.772
No, they already
powered it up. It didn't work.

846
01:30:47.856 --> 01:30:51.314
-Maybe the live came loose?
-That's not the problem.

847
01:30:51.397 --> 01:30:54.606
-Let's check the live--
-That's not the problem, Alex!

848
01:30:55.439 --> 01:30:57.522
We'll have to open the valve by hand.

849
01:31:02.564 --> 01:31:06.022
Let's go. We have to go down to the valve.

850
01:31:07.689 --> 01:31:10.064
-Boris…
-Let's go, guys.

851
01:31:10.147 --> 01:31:11.481
-Boris?
-No, Comrade Stysin.

852
01:31:11.564 --> 01:31:16.064
-We must get Boris out.
-It's so hot in here, Mom…

853
01:31:16.147 --> 01:31:17.147
Boris?

854
01:31:29.231 --> 01:31:30.314
Where's Nikita?

855
01:31:36.564 --> 01:31:38.106
Where's Nikita?

856
01:31:42.731 --> 01:31:44.689
-I left my flashlight. I'll go get it.
-Nikita!

857
01:31:44.772 --> 01:31:45.981
Be quick.

858
01:32:10.439 --> 01:32:11.356
Almost there.

859
01:32:19.981 --> 01:32:21.022
Did you hear that?

860
01:32:25.147 --> 01:32:26.064
Hear what?

861
01:32:28.981 --> 01:32:29.814
Water.

862
01:32:32.314 --> 01:32:33.314
Over there.

863
01:32:35.731 --> 01:32:37.772
Boris, take it easy.

864
01:32:38.856 --> 01:32:40.647
We're getting out of here.

865
01:32:45.272 --> 01:32:48.356
But this is the corridor
that goes straight to the valve.

866
01:32:49.272 --> 01:32:50.272
Let's go.

867
01:32:50.856 --> 01:32:52.856
Boris, wait. Boris!

868
01:32:53.939 --> 01:32:56.439
Wait! Boris, stop!

869
01:33:01.189 --> 01:33:02.189
Alex, you okay?

870
01:33:03.772 --> 01:33:06.647
-Go after him.
-Boris! Damn you!

871
01:33:06.731 --> 01:33:07.897
Boris!

872
01:33:10.564 --> 01:33:12.981
Boris, it's too close to the reactor!

873
01:33:14.397 --> 01:33:16.897
Stop! Stop right there!

874
01:33:18.314 --> 01:33:20.272
It's too close to the reactor, Boris!

875
01:33:35.564 --> 01:33:37.106
There's light ahead.

876
01:33:38.772 --> 01:33:42.022
-Stop! Boris!
-I see light!

877
01:33:43.731 --> 01:33:46.022
Guys, there's light ahead!

878
01:33:47.522 --> 01:33:48.981
I see light!

879
01:33:52.439 --> 01:33:55.731
Stop!

880
01:34:05.981 --> 01:34:06.856
Stop!

881
01:34:21.064 --> 01:34:24.147
Close the door! You'll burn to death!

882
01:34:42.106 --> 01:34:44.856
ENTRANCE

883
01:34:48.981 --> 01:34:50.314
Easy, Boris. Hang on.

884
01:34:50.397 --> 01:34:52.397
Alex!

885
01:34:54.689 --> 01:34:55.689
Alex!

886
01:34:57.981 --> 01:34:58.814
Quick!

887
01:35:01.272 --> 01:35:02.397
There's magma there.

888
01:35:03.231 --> 01:35:05.689
Magma. We have to get out.

889
01:35:08.356 --> 01:35:09.689
We've got to get out.

890
01:35:19.064 --> 01:35:20.522
Nikita… Where's Nikita?

891
01:35:22.064 --> 01:35:24.647
Get their clothes off
and get them to decontamination, now!

892
01:35:29.897 --> 01:35:32.106
There's magma there. Magma.

893
01:35:33.814 --> 01:35:35.689
Comrade Stysin…

894
01:35:39.439 --> 01:35:42.647
Let's go back down.
We need to open the valve.

895
01:35:42.731 --> 01:35:44.231
There's water in the corridors.

896
01:35:44.314 --> 01:35:46.981
Take it easy, Valery.
You've done your job.

897
01:35:47.064 --> 01:35:48.689
Call for a helicopter.

898
01:36:27.439 --> 01:36:28.981
How much did Boris get?

899
01:36:29.689 --> 01:36:31.147
Seven hundred rem. Perhaps more.

900
01:36:46.231 --> 01:36:49.772
They're sending liquidators
back in to carry on their work.

901
01:37:34.356 --> 01:37:35.397
Comrade Stysin.

902
01:37:45.231 --> 01:37:46.772
You'll have to come with us.

903
01:37:48.522 --> 01:37:50.147
Are you taking me in?

904
01:37:50.231 --> 01:37:51.189
Only for a talk.

905
01:37:51.272 --> 01:37:54.814
Just stand there, and listen quietly
while they dress you down.

906
01:37:58.231 --> 01:37:59.564
I won't listen quietly.

907
01:38:00.564 --> 01:38:02.272
Maybe your plan is better than mine.

908
01:38:02.356 --> 01:38:03.689
You wanna take a bunch of people

909
01:38:03.772 --> 01:38:05.606
and use them
to plug the hole in the reactor.

910
01:38:06.314 --> 01:38:09.481
We should've thought better
when they were building the damned thing,

911
01:38:09.564 --> 01:38:12.814
but we allowed it
to be built so that it would blow up.

912
01:38:14.272 --> 01:38:16.522
That's what I'm going to tell them.

913
01:38:17.272 --> 01:38:19.356
They can cover their asses all they want.

914
01:38:20.397 --> 01:38:22.564
Why don't you just mind your own business?

915
01:38:23.272 --> 01:38:25.481
Who are you fighting?

916
01:38:25.564 --> 01:38:28.147
The system? It's like radiation.

917
01:38:28.231 --> 01:38:32.189
Invisible, ever-present, and everlasting.

918
01:38:32.272 --> 01:38:33.647
Stop acting like a child.

919
01:38:36.064 --> 01:38:37.439
But I am a child.

920
01:38:39.856 --> 01:38:41.772
I'm a child of the Soviet regime.

921
01:39:30.272 --> 01:39:37.231
WARD NO. 2

922
01:39:44.314 --> 01:39:45.731
How are you feeling?

923
01:39:47.231 --> 01:39:49.356
-Fine.
-Get back in bed.

924
01:39:49.439 --> 01:39:50.522
How's Nikita?

925
01:39:50.606 --> 01:39:51.606
He's fine.

926
01:39:52.981 --> 01:39:56.272
Doctor, I'd like to have
five minutes with Alexey if that's okay.

927
01:39:57.564 --> 01:39:59.856
-You have five minutes.
-Thank you.

928
01:40:02.189 --> 01:40:03.272
Is that your mother?

929
01:40:04.272 --> 01:40:05.897
Why is she crying? You're alive.

930
01:40:07.939 --> 01:40:10.147
I'm gonna go down to open the valve.

931
01:40:16.981 --> 01:40:18.564
That's a suicide mission.

932
01:40:26.897 --> 01:40:28.522
There aren't enough volunteers.

933
01:40:29.481 --> 01:40:30.939
None, to be more precise.

934
01:40:32.231 --> 01:40:35.022
Only soldiers.
There's more than enough of them.

935
01:40:36.272 --> 01:40:37.647
But they're not volunteers.

936
01:40:38.606 --> 01:40:39.439
Yeah.

937
01:40:41.022 --> 01:40:42.439
They don't get much choice.

938
01:40:48.356 --> 01:40:49.981
Maybe they'll find another way?

939
01:40:50.564 --> 01:40:51.939
They can blow a hole in it…

940
01:40:52.647 --> 01:40:53.981
or pump the water out.

941
01:40:56.647 --> 01:40:58.272
Maybe they'll blow a hole in it.

942
01:41:00.022 --> 01:41:01.314
Maybe they won't.

943
01:41:05.022 --> 01:41:08.189
If whatever they do
doesn't work, it'll blow a hole in itself.

944
01:41:27.647 --> 01:41:30.189
Right. I'll go back to my mom.

945
01:41:56.439 --> 01:41:58.606
You're done. Call the next one in.

946
01:43:07.397 --> 01:43:08.397
Hi, Olga.

947
01:43:30.814 --> 01:43:32.856
Why did you leave us?

948
01:43:32.939 --> 01:43:35.064
Why did you leave me back then?

949
01:43:35.147 --> 01:43:36.356
Why?

950
01:44:01.856 --> 01:44:03.689
I don't know what's wrong with him.

951
01:44:04.439 --> 01:44:06.106
They won't let me see him.

952
01:44:07.606 --> 01:44:10.272
I'm cutting hair here, so stupid…

953
01:44:21.856 --> 01:44:24.439
Right now, you and I
are going to go and get him.

954
01:44:26.481 --> 01:44:28.231
We'll put him on a plane to Switzerland.

955
01:44:28.772 --> 01:44:30.814
He'll get proper treatment there.

956
01:44:37.189 --> 01:44:38.897
What? What plane?

957
01:44:39.856 --> 01:44:42.439
I got him a seat
on a charter flight for radiation victims.

958
01:44:43.981 --> 01:44:45.814
What's wrong with him? Why Switzerland?

959
01:44:45.897 --> 01:44:49.564
Their doctors are better than ours.
It's the best possible option for him.

960
01:44:52.272 --> 01:44:54.272
He's going to be fine.

961
01:44:56.856 --> 01:44:58.647
We just have to get him…

962
01:44:59.856 --> 01:45:01.397
and put him on the plane.

963
01:45:55.606 --> 01:45:57.522
My boy, please forgive me.

964
01:45:57.606 --> 01:45:59.356
They wouldn't let me see you.

965
01:45:59.439 --> 01:46:02.439
You got to ride
with flashing lights, just like Gorbachev.

966
01:46:03.064 --> 01:46:05.189
Don't be scared.
You're going to get better there.

967
01:46:05.272 --> 01:46:06.647
Alexey Savostin?

968
01:46:07.356 --> 01:46:09.314
Yes, there's our little soldier.

969
01:46:09.397 --> 01:46:11.314
Please give me
your little soldier's documents

970
01:46:11.397 --> 01:46:12.606
and say your goodbyes.

971
01:46:13.689 --> 01:46:16.397
Will there be any doctors
who speak Russian over there?

972
01:46:16.481 --> 01:46:17.564
I'll be there.

973
01:46:19.897 --> 01:46:21.147
I love you, sweetie.

974
01:46:21.856 --> 01:46:23.231
Why are you leaving me?

975
01:46:25.314 --> 01:46:27.439
I'm not allowed to go with you.

976
01:46:27.522 --> 01:46:28.481
Don't leave me, Mom!

977
01:46:29.064 --> 01:46:29.897
Olga…

978
01:46:32.147 --> 01:46:33.231
Mom!

979
01:46:51.064 --> 01:46:52.231
Let's go.

980
01:47:26.481 --> 01:47:27.356
Olga, sit down.

981
01:47:50.897 --> 01:47:52.397
We didn't ask for the phone number.

982
01:47:52.481 --> 01:47:53.481
I'll get it.

983
01:47:55.564 --> 01:47:57.314
We have to call him every day.

984
01:48:02.731 --> 01:48:04.897
You've done
everything you could. Now relax.

985
01:48:06.522 --> 01:48:09.147
When he gets back,
he needs you to be strong for him.

986
01:48:12.689 --> 01:48:13.731
You're right.

987
01:48:15.897 --> 01:48:16.772
Thank you.

988
01:48:19.439 --> 01:48:21.314
I promised to be there for you, didn't I?

989
01:48:40.439 --> 01:48:41.814
I feel bad for how I treated you.

990
01:48:42.814 --> 01:48:43.939
And I'm scared.

991
01:48:46.106 --> 01:48:47.647
It's me who should feel bad.

992
01:49:17.689 --> 01:49:18.564
Alex.

993
01:49:25.731 --> 01:49:26.814
Alex.

994
01:49:42.439 --> 01:49:43.356
Alex, no.

995
01:50:03.397 --> 01:50:07.981
The Soviet nation
celebrates this year's May Day,

996
01:50:08.064 --> 01:50:12.606
full of vigor and creative energy.

997
01:50:13.314 --> 01:50:16.814
Festive crowds walked along Khreschatyk,

998
01:50:16.897 --> 01:50:19.314
Kiev's main thoroughfare.

999
01:50:19.897 --> 01:50:22.981
Tens of thousands
of people took part in the parade…

1000
01:50:58.689 --> 01:50:59.856
Alex?

1001
01:51:05.564 --> 01:51:06.397
Alex?

1002
01:51:16.772 --> 01:51:20.356
Olga, I'm sorry for leaving you again,
but I have to go back in there.

1003
01:51:20.439 --> 01:51:23.856
You have the best son in the world.
And you picked the best name for him!

1004
01:51:38.189 --> 01:51:39.731
I'm glad you volunteered.

1005
01:51:42.147 --> 01:51:44.064
I wish I could say the same.

1006
01:51:45.981 --> 01:51:49.606
Turns out I lied to you. We won't get
our victory lap around Red Square.

1007
01:51:50.272 --> 01:51:51.939
You're an idiot, Alex.

1008
01:51:54.356 --> 01:51:57.439
It's a shame Boris didn't make it
to see this historic moment.

1009
01:52:02.231 --> 01:52:04.439
It's a good thing
Alex can't talk underwater.

1010
01:53:05.064 --> 01:53:06.147
This way.

1011
01:53:31.314 --> 01:53:34.731
The water's almost 60C… like they said.

1012
01:53:36.064 --> 01:53:39.106
Valery… since nobody can hear us here…

1013
01:53:41.064 --> 01:53:43.147
why did this thing really blow up?

1014
01:53:44.856 --> 01:53:46.147
Because of people.

1015
01:53:50.397 --> 01:53:51.814
Which people exactly?

1016
01:53:56.481 --> 01:53:57.897
Does it matter?

1017
01:54:09.564 --> 01:54:10.606
You ready? Let's go.

1018
01:55:16.606 --> 01:55:17.606
What's the matter?

1019
01:55:19.689 --> 01:55:22.939
I'm not scared,
my hands are just shaking like crazy.

1020
01:55:24.272 --> 01:55:27.272
I'll open the valve myself.
I can't wait any longer, it's too hot.

1021
01:55:27.356 --> 01:55:28.814
Wait for me.

1022
01:55:32.231 --> 01:55:33.314
I can't.

1023
01:58:18.939 --> 01:58:20.814
Ivan, the water's draining.

1024
01:58:32.522 --> 01:58:34.397
The water's draining. They did it.

1025
02:03:40.606 --> 02:03:43.814
They found him after the water drained.
Everyone thought he was dead.

1026
02:03:49.856 --> 02:03:50.939
How do I look?

1027
02:03:52.981 --> 02:03:54.314
Good enough.

1028
02:04:01.814 --> 02:04:03.397
Why don't you take him to Kiev?

1029
02:04:06.439 --> 02:04:09.814
Three hours of being rattled around
on the road won't do him any good.

1030
02:04:11.814 --> 02:04:12.897
Listen.

1031
02:04:16.856 --> 02:04:18.064
He's radioactive.

1032
02:04:18.147 --> 02:04:21.022
Keep contact to a minimum.
It could be very dangerous.

1033
02:04:31.981 --> 02:04:33.356
ISOLATION WARD - STAFF ONLY

1034
02:04:51.606 --> 02:04:58.564
KEEP OUT

1035
02:07:15.314 --> 02:07:19.189
THREE MONTHS LATER

1036
02:09:44.522 --> 02:09:51.481
DEDICATED TO THE CHERNOBYL LIQUIDATORS
